{"author":{"id":"fd7f3dbc4355c59607d7a10ce53dc23877e6b88e93fde4f9e421c07a3df0b23b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791190492,"nonce":"elCXzCjA6BX3zXyAGzQ/ibnhjBQ=","metadata":{"github-url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/33","origin":"github","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"I_kwDOULtcMc8AAAABVEsTPg","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:labels":"","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:number":"33","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:status":"open","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"6c94016feac383ef9975db8b11866b41a60379248d6f769839329991e985a13c","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:title":"Refreshing page removes everything or make the \"save\" feature more readable or make an autro save on input field","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:url":"https://github.com/EPFL-ENAC/vps-mitsi/issues/33"},"title":"Refreshing page removes everything or make the \"save\" feature more readable or make an autro save on input field","message":"**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\nCurrently, changes persist when navigating between tabs, but they are all lost when the page is reloaded. This is surprising behaviour, and it can cause users to lose a substantial amount of information they have already filled in.\n\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\nChanges should persist both when switching tabs and when reloading the page. Since changes would then be saved automatically, the \"Save\" button should be removed.\n\nThis helps users because they no longer risk losing their work through an accidental or intentional reload, and they don't have to remember to save manually.\n\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\n- Keeping the \"Save\" button and showing a warning before the page is reloaded when there are unsaved changes. This prevents accidental loss but still relies on the user saving manually.\n- Keeping the \"Save\" button alongside automatic persistence. This would be redundant and could confuse users about whether their changes are already saved.\n\n**Additional context**\nThe current behaviour is inconsistent: changes survive tab navigation, which suggests they are saved, but they do not survive a reload.","files":null}]}